meta {
  name: 32 Update Overall Result
  type: http
  seq: 32
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/overall-result
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "templateId": "{{overallResultTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Apply an Overall Result template to a report, or edit its already-applied
  content in place — two mutually exclusive actions on the same endpoint,
  distinguished by which single field is sent:

  - `templateId` only (apply): the server resolves the named
    `OverallResultTemplate`'s CURRENT `content` itself — it never trusts a
    client-supplied content string for an apply — and snapshots that content
    onto this report, alongside `templateId` (so the UI can show which
    template is active). 404 `OVERALL_RESULT_TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUND` if the id
    doesn't resolve to an active template in this tenant.

    ```json
    { "templateId": "{{overallResultTemplateId}}" }
    ```

  - `content` only (edit): overwrites the report's `overallResultContent`
    in place (post-apply technician edits, e.g. filling in a value the
    template left blank). `overallResultTemplateId` is left untouched, so
    the UI still shows which template this report started from even after
    the edited content diverges from that template's own current text.

    ```json
    { "content": "<p>Overall result: Normal.</p>" }
    ```

  Sending BOTH `templateId` and `content` in the same request, or NEITHER,
  is rejected with 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR` — exactly one of the two is
  required per call.

  Gated by `TechnicianSetting.isOverallResultEditable` (default `false`,
  see "Technician Settings" module). When the toggle is off, this is a
  **silent no-op**: the request succeeds (200) but returns the report's
  current, unchanged overall result — it does NOT reject the request. Turn
  the toggle on first if a write doesn't seem to be taking effect.

  Response shape: `{ "templateId": string | null, "content": string | null }`
  — the report's overall result state after the write (or after the no-op,
  if the toggle is off).

  ⚠️ Known gap (tracked, not yet fixed): unlike every other mutating action
  on this report, this endpoint does NOT check `LabReportStatus` — a
  PUBLISHED report's overall result can still be edited through this route.
  The only guard that applies is the lock check below. Do not rely on
  publish-immutability for this one field yet.

  404 `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` if missing/other-tenant/other-branch. 409
  `LAB_REPORT_LOCKED` if the report is locked (`lock()`'d via
  `POST /lab-reports/:id/lock`) — this is the only lifecycle gate currently
  enforced here.

  Requires `LAB_EDIT_REPORT` (unlike this module's read-only
  `GET /overall-result-templates*` routes, which are open to any
  authenticated business user with the Technician module enabled).
}
